<p>In this problem, we already know the sum we=E2=80=99re looking for (k), =
meaning our goal is to find:</p>
<ul>
<li>All pairs of <code>i</code> and <code>j</code> such that <strong><code>=
prefix_sum[j] - prefix_sum[i - 1] =3D=3D k</code></strong> when <code>i &gt=
; 0</code>.</li>
<li>All values of <code>j</code> such that <strong><code>prefix_sum[j] =3D=
=3D k</code></strong> when <code>i =3D=3D 0</code>.</li>
</ul>
<p>We can unify both cases by recognizing that the formula prefix_sum[j] =
=3D=3D k is the same as the formula <code>prefix_sum[j] - prefix_sum[i - 1]=
