/p>
<p>Therefore, for each prefix sum (<code>curr_prefix_sum</code>), we need t=
o find the number of times <code>curr_prefix_sum - k</code> previously appe=
ared as a prefix sum before.</p>
<p>This is similar to the problem presented in <em>Pair Sum - Unsorted</em>=
 in the <em>Hash Maps and Sets</em> chapter, where we learn a <strong>hash =
map</strong> is useful for implementing the above idea efficiently. In this=
 context, if we store encountered prefix sum values in a hash map, we can c=
heck if <code>curr_prefix_sum - k</code> was encountered before in constant=
 time.</p>
<p>Note, it's also important to track the frequency of each prefix sum we e=
ncounter using the hash map, as the same prefix sum may appear multiple tim=
es.</p>
